{"type": "tool_call", "n": 7, "ts": 1790153758.9975839, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "MEMO \u2014 UK Travel (GL 6300) Q1 2026 spend analysis\nPrepared by: david.murguia@gmail.com | Date: 2026-04-03\nRequest: UK MD asked what the UK entity spent on travel in Q1 2026 (GBP) and which merchant accounts for the most.\n\nRESULT\nUK GL 6300 (Travel), functional currency GBP, Q1 2026 total = GBP 4,591.73 across 19 entries.\n  Jan 2026: 1,376.38\n  Feb 2026: 1,649.47\n  Mar 2026: 1,565.88\nTies to GL: account 6300 cumulative ending balance at 2026-03-31 = 4,591.73 debit; no opening balance at 1 Jan 2026, so period activity = cumulative.\n\nBY MERCHANT (per entry memos)\n  British Airways (airfare)   3,669.27   79.9%\n  Premier Inn (hotel)           460.98   10.0%\n  Addison Lee (taxi)            348.58    7.6%\n  Trainline (rail)              112.90    2.5%\n  Total                       4,591.73  100.0%\n\nANSWER: British Airways is the largest merchant at GBP 3,669.27, ~80% of Q1 UK travel spend. Three London-New York bookings alone total GBP 1,940.40 (42% of all Q1 travel).\n\nSUPPORTING ENTRIES\nBritish Airways: JE-00041 (01-08, 182.55), JE-00072 (01-21, 640.00), JE-00083 (01-24, 149.80), JE-00142 (02-06, 145.52), JE-00151 (02-09, 453.38), JE-00166 (02-17, 712.40), JE-00230 (03-02, 451.50), JE-00257 (03-10, 588.00), JE-00275 (03-19, 346.12).\nPremier Inn: JE-00074 (01-21, 238.65), JE-00145 (02-07, 222.33).\nAddison Lee: JE-00042 (01-08, 65.82), JE-00046 (01-10, 24.60), JE-00097 (01-27, 74.96), JE-00127 (02-03, 70.13), JE-00172 (02-19, 45.71), JE-00258 (03-11, 32.48), JE-00285 (03-23, 34.88).\nTrainline: JE-00246 (03-07, 112.90).\n\nCAVEATS\n1. The March 2026 close is still in progress; the March figure of 1,565.88 is preliminary and could change if late expense reports or travel accruals are posted before sign-off.\n2. All 19 entries originate from the corporate card feed (source=card, posted_by=card.sync), debiting 6300 and crediting 1000 Cash - Operating. All carry attached support. Spot-checked the two largest: JE-00166 (712.40, support DOC-0123) and JE-00257 (588.00, support DOC-0182) - both agree to memo, amount and account coding.\n\nACTIONS TAKEN\nRead-only analysis. No journal entries posted, no reclassifications made, no exceptions flagged - nothing in the population was unsupported or required adjustment.\n"}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 10}
